# The SciGraphs byte-by-byte conformance matrix: all 32 `apply_graph_layout` names against the
# motor layout each is supposed to be, over one fixture set both arms read, measured in Python
# and judged in graph-cli against the pinned baseline (docs/measurements/scigraphs-conformance.md).
# Six steps across three images, so it is a script and not a single command.
scigraphs-conformance|0|scripts/scigraphs-conformance.sh
# The negative control. `--break` re-emits with GM_MUTATE_SCIGRAPHS_CONFORMANCE=SPRING_3D, which
# flips one bit (bit 29, the last an f32 keeps) of one f64 coordinate in that one row's file,
# and re-runs every arm. Exactly one row must then fail and it must be SPRING_3D: a control
# that moved nothing, or moved more than one row, would exit 0 here and the gate would be
# measuring nothing.
negctl-scigraphs-conformance|nonzero|scripts/scigraphs-conformance.sh --break

# The supply-chain gate (scripts/orch/rows/audit.rows): RustSec advisories, the SPDX allow list,
# duplicate versions and crate provenance over both lockfiles, plus the shipped bundle's runtime
# deps. Each row needs the network (the advisory-db clone, the registry advisory endpoint), so it
# can turn red with no change in the tree the day an advisory is published; an offline host is a
# fetch failure in the log, not a finding. The controls break the policy itself.
cargo-deny-motor|0|GR_IMAGE=ge-audit scripts/orch/gr cargo deny --manifest-path Cargo.toml check advisories bans licenses sources
cargo-deny-server|0|GR_IMAGE=ge-audit scripts/orch/gr cargo deny --manifest-path server/Cargo.toml --config deny.toml check advisories bans licenses sources
npm-audit-app|0|scripts/orch/node-slim.sh bash -c 'cd app && npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high'
